WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.597
This challenge asks for patients whose admission count is above the average admission count among patients who

00:00:07.597 --> 00:00:09.922
have at least one admission.

00:00:09.922 --> 00:00:10.562
Break the task into stages.

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:12.807
First create patient-level admission counts.

00:00:12.807 --> 00:00:15.557
Then calculate the average of those counts.

00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:19.122
Finally compare each patient's count with that average.

00:00:19.122 --> 00:00:24.942
Use the starter and test the query incrementally rather than writing everything at once.

00:00:24.942 --> 00:00:27.947
ANY and ALL compare one value with a set.

00:00:27.947 --> 00:00:32.462
ANY needs the comparison to succeed against at least one returned value;

00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:36.307
ALL requires it to succeed against every returned value.

00:00:36.307 --> 00:00:43.439
Empty sets and NULLs can affect the result, so test those cases explicitly when the set is data-driven.
